# Pre-release iteration

Read and follow the PRE-RELEASE iteration policy and scoped validation in `AGENTS.md`.
This project has NO EXTERNAL PRODUCTION and is NOT SHIPPING until the user explicitly requests release hardening.

- Run focused affected tests/typechecks and meaningful test-first bug regressions.
- Batch related work on the existing branch/worktree; avoid a PR per chunk and automatic multiple review seats.
- Use one proportionate review for auth, storage, protocol, or concurrency risk.
- For ordinary UI work, avoid repeated full monorepo/browser/Swift/Rust/native/emulator/multi-OS checks.
- Run a small relevant local test/build, then commit/push when authorized and respond to feedback.
- Keep optional checks asynchronous and nonblocking unless the risk requires them.
- Merge/push main directly when authorized; use PRs only when requested or required.
- Honor actual branch protection and later explicit user instructions; queued optional checks are not merge gates.
- Preserve user data, secrets, authentication guarantees, and package boundaries.
- Full CI and native CHD acceptance remain available by manual workflow dispatch.
